  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Amtec is a federal contractor with $283M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Amtec won 15 awards so far this fiscal year with an average award size of $18.9M. Obligations fell 29.5% year over year. Historical obligations show variation by fiscal year: FY21 was $248M, FY22 was $70.4M, FY23 was $138M, FY24 was $513M, FY25 was $401M, and FY26 is $283M. The current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is still in progress, and the listed award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than obligations. Readers should note that the page summarizes obligations rather than total contract ceilings. The mix of award count and average award size indicates a program of relatively large individual awards this fiscal year compared with FY22 and FY23. Procurement officers and contractors looking at Amtec can use the year-by-year obligations to identify when the company saw major increases and declines in federal funding without inferring future performance or contract details.",
